    "result_text": "There's only one test class in the project, and the full suite passes.\n\nDone. The change is implemented and all tests are green.\n\n## What I did\n\nThe `getOwner` endpoint returns an `OwnerDto` produced by MapStruct's `OwnerMapper`, and the DTO is generated from `openapi.yml`. I followed the existing `displayName` pattern (a computed, read-only field) to add `initials`:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `initials` property to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` has the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a mapping expression computing initials from the model:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"initials\", expression = \"java(owner.getFirstName().substring(0, 1).toUpperCase() + \\\".\\\" + owner.getLastName().substring(0, 1).toUpperCase() + \\\".\\\")\")\n   ```\n\n`firstName`/`lastName` are `@NotEmpty`, so the `substring(0,1)` is safe. For `\"john\"`/`\"smith\"` this yields `\"J.S.\"`, matching the acceptance test (`$.initials == \"J.S.\"`).\n\nTest run: `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.",
